# ========================================
# Notion Integration (Optional)
# ========================================
#
# IMPORTANT: This is for APP OWNERS only, not end users!
#
# If you want to enable Notion sync for your users:
# 1. Create ONE Notion integration at: https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
# 2. Add these environment variables to your deployment
# 3. All your users will connect through YOUR integration
#
# If you DON'T set these up, users can still use the app - they just won't
# see the Notion login option and will use local storage only.
#
# ========================================

NEXT_PUBLIC_NOTION_CLIENT_ID=your_notion_client_id_here
NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET=your_notion_client_secret_here

# ========================================
# Setup Instructions for App Owners:
# ========================================
#
# 1. Go to https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
# 2. Click "+ New integration"
# 3. Give it a name (e.g., "Cushion Savings Tracker")
# 4. Select capabilities: Read content, Update content, Insert content
# 5. Set Type: Public
# 6. Add Redirect URIs:
#    - Development: http://localhost:3000/api/notion/callback
#    - Production: https://yourdomain.com/api/notion/callback
# 7. Copy the OAuth client ID and paste above as NEXT_PUBLIC_NOTION_CLIENT_ID
# 8. Copy the OAuth client secret and paste above as NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET
# 9. Rename this file to .env.local (for local dev) or add to your hosting platform's environment variables
#
# ========================================
# For Deployment (Vercel, Netlify, etc.):
# ========================================
#
# Add these two environment variables in your hosting platform:
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_NOTION_CLIENT_ID (your integration's client ID)
# - NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET (your integration's client secret)
#
# Don't forget to add your production URL to the Redirect URIs in Notion!
#
# ========================================
